WEBVTT

00:20.760 --> 00:21.600
Hmm!

00:21.800 --> 00:23.200
- You liked it?
- Hmm!

00:23.800 --> 00:25.240
Very tasty! Thank you!

00:25.480 --> 00:26.560
Thank you so much.

00:27.440 --> 00:29.200
I also love what you've
done with the place.

00:29.480 --> 00:30.960
- It's all you.
- Of course.

00:31.520 --> 00:33.080
What's your reaction
to moving house?

00:33.360 --> 00:35.760
It's fine. It’s just that
the house is a bit small.

00:35.840 --> 00:37.320
"A bit small?"

00:37.840 --> 00:39.520
I'll have a palace built for you.

00:39.760 --> 00:41.840
Zee, could you give me some money
to build a palace for my son?

00:41.960 --> 00:43.000
- Just a minute.
- Come on.

00:43.120 --> 00:45.520
Whose house is this, son?

00:52.520 --> 00:53.840
Dad, it's our house.

00:55.480 --> 00:58.640
Did NBIDC give us a new house?

01:03.840 --> 01:05.240
Dad, we're in Bombay.

01:06.040 --> 01:08.720
We were in Navi Mumbai, weren't we?

01:08.760 --> 01:09.880
Now we're in Bombay, Dad.

01:14.240 --> 01:18.040
Do you work at NBIDC as well?

01:18.160 --> 01:20.000
Dad, he's Xerxes,

01:20.800 --> 01:23.720
my senior, and we work at Tata.

01:26.560 --> 01:28.080
- Namaste, Uncle.
- Namaste.

01:29.640 --> 01:31.880
Dad, please sit
and have lunch with us.

01:32.520 --> 01:33.920
No, Kumud.

01:34.240 --> 01:36.280
Please bring my food to my room.

01:36.480 --> 01:37.760
- Okay?
- Okay.

01:39.000 --> 01:40.320
Bye, Mr. 'Jersey'.

01:40.440 --> 01:41.400
Bye, Uncle.

01:42.440 --> 01:43.360
Bye.

01:43.440 --> 01:44.560
Excuse me.

01:50.000 --> 01:51.000
Do you want something?

01:51.320 --> 01:52.520
No, thank you.

01:54.520 --> 01:56.360
We're planning our future,

01:57.600 --> 01:59.880
but my dad is forgetting the past.

02:03.640 --> 02:05.200
He's gradually forgetting
everything.

02:36.440 --> 02:38.520
'Mr. Desai and Akash's company'

02:38.720 --> 02:41.400
'was still in the project phase.'

02:41.920 --> 02:43.000
'The Watch Project.'

02:43.800 --> 02:48.000
'There was still time for the
project to develop into a company.'

02:48.920 --> 02:50.480
'Step 1-Research.'

02:50.800 --> 02:51.600
'What kind of research?'

02:51.920 --> 02:55.360
'Market research, product analysis,
and customer base.'

02:55.640 --> 02:58.400
'They had to visit different places
to do the ground research.'

02:58.680 --> 03:00.920
'Only then could they move
to the next step.'

03:01.880 --> 03:03.120
'And it was Step 2-Employees.'

03:04.600 --> 03:06.040
'Sikha Agarwal.'

03:07.160 --> 03:08.880
'Nikhil Sharma.'

03:11.040 --> 03:12.480
'Tanya Singh.'

03:14.080 --> 03:16.520
Tanya, sell us this paper.

03:16.920 --> 03:20.400
Sir, I'm here to sell watches,
not paper.

03:22.040 --> 03:25.360
I can give a 90% discount
on this paper.

03:25.600 --> 03:27.680
Are you planning to make
the company incur a loss?

03:27.800 --> 03:28.640
No! No! No!

03:28.800 --> 03:30.480
Your company might incur a loss

03:30.560 --> 03:32.000
if you don't hire me.

03:33.000 --> 03:35.200
Such overconfidence is not good.

03:35.360 --> 03:36.800
Sir, I'm confident

03:36.880 --> 03:38.760
in demonstrating the product
qualities to the customers.

03:38.840 --> 03:40.000
"Our product is really nice."

03:40.320 --> 03:42.520
Saying that is not enough
for the customers.

03:43.280 --> 03:44.320
What about relatability?

03:44.400 --> 03:45.240
That's the point!

03:45.320 --> 03:47.600
A discount
convinces people immediately.

03:47.680 --> 03:49.440
And that's relatability.

03:49.520 --> 03:50.720
At least try it once.

03:50.840 --> 03:52.000
Please sell us this paper.

03:53.440 --> 03:54.840
If I tell you my secret,

03:54.920 --> 03:56.840
it will be a loss for me, so...

03:57.400 --> 03:58.240
Huh?

03:58.840 --> 04:02.080
If the task is to sell
this piece of paper,

04:03.160 --> 04:04.320
then...

04:04.800 --> 04:05.880
Sir, the Four Ps.

04:06.120 --> 04:08.480
CRM and KPIs
can help us win the world.

04:08.560 --> 04:10.000
What does CRM stand for?

04:10.080 --> 04:11.360
CRM, sir...

04:11.480 --> 04:13.680
Try hiring someone else in my place.

04:13.800 --> 04:16.520
Then you'll regret not hiring me.

04:16.840 --> 04:18.640
Okay, we'll hire someone else.
Thank you!

04:20.040 --> 04:20.960
Excuse me?

04:21.160 --> 04:22.200
A 50% discount.

04:27.040 --> 04:28.600
'C', 'R', 'M'...

04:28.760 --> 04:29.560
"CRM."

04:29.640 --> 04:31.000
- A 30% discount.
- Huh?

04:35.920 --> 04:37.880
- Consumer...
- "Consumer."

04:40.440 --> 04:41.640
A 10% discount?

04:42.480 --> 04:44.800
Sir, CRM stands for...
I can't remember.

04:45.600 --> 04:47.000
- Should I leave?
- Oh, yes!

04:55.240 --> 04:57.080
What are you trying to say?

04:57.640 --> 04:59.240
Multipurpose, sir.

04:59.720 --> 05:03.280
People... Especially Indians.

05:03.600 --> 05:05.680
If we show them
the multiple benefits of a product,

05:05.880 --> 05:09.720
in addition to its primary use,

05:10.040 --> 05:11.160
they are more likely to buy it.

05:11.280 --> 05:13.760
What multiple advantages of a watch

05:14.200 --> 05:15.360
can you show the customers?

05:16.400 --> 05:20.160
Sir, in practical terms,
a watch only tells the time.

05:20.960 --> 05:25.240
But if I give this watch
to my daughter,

05:25.760 --> 05:27.680
it will become
a cherished memory for her.

05:28.080 --> 05:30.200
And when she gives it to her
daughter, it will become a legacy.

05:30.640 --> 05:33.560
And if I give it
to my company's employee,

05:33.640 --> 05:36.600
this watch will become
their goodwill or pride.

05:40.640 --> 05:42.880
Sir, the customers
will come to buy a watch,

05:43.160 --> 05:45.920
but will leave with a feeling

05:46.680 --> 05:47.960
of a deep connection.

05:52.280 --> 05:53.120
Hmm.

05:55.040 --> 05:58.280
So, Miss Megha Mhatre,

06:02.600 --> 06:03.560
we'll be in touch.

06:04.120 --> 06:05.000
Thank you.

06:05.520 --> 06:06.680
Thank you, sir.

06:10.520 --> 06:12.240
- It's already five.
- Hmm.

06:15.440 --> 06:16.640
Sir, these are the resumes.

06:16.880 --> 06:18.280
Candidates are waiting outside.

06:23.360 --> 06:24.400
Oi, Zee.

06:25.080 --> 06:26.920
How will we interview
so many engineers?

06:27.000 --> 06:28.800
- It's already five o'clock.
- Hmm.

06:29.200 --> 06:30.240
They are twelve.

06:42.240 --> 06:44.200
Let's have a demonstration
instead of a discussion.

06:59.720 --> 07:00.960
If the fan works,

07:01.600 --> 07:02.560
the job is yours.

07:03.040 --> 07:03.840
Sir,

07:04.600 --> 07:07.000
will an electrician's task

07:07.360 --> 07:08.960
judge the capability of engineers?

07:09.040 --> 07:11.120
If you don't want the job,

07:11.440 --> 07:12.480
you may leave.

07:15.160 --> 07:16.120
Anyone?

07:16.400 --> 07:17.240
Good.

07:17.520 --> 07:18.720
Kindly take your positions.

07:19.040 --> 07:20.600
Your time starts now!

07:43.920 --> 07:46.280
- Whoa!
- Please be careful, my friend!

07:46.440 --> 07:47.880
Be careful, guys!

07:54.080 --> 07:55.000
Whoa!

07:56.240 --> 07:57.240
Relax.

08:27.800 --> 08:28.800
Okay, guys.

08:31.160 --> 08:32.040
Ten...

08:34.480 --> 08:35.400
Nine...

08:38.400 --> 08:39.240
Eight...

08:41.480 --> 08:42.600
Seven...

08:43.960 --> 08:44.880
Six...

08:46.840 --> 08:47.880
Five...

08:49.040 --> 08:50.040
Four!

08:50.440 --> 08:51.280
Three...

08:52.120 --> 08:53.080
Two...

08:54.240 --> 08:55.360
One! Time's up!

08:57.760 --> 08:59.000
You just made it.

08:59.920 --> 09:02.800
Sir, please turn on the fans.

09:06.400 --> 09:07.320
Whoa!

09:07.600 --> 09:08.440
God!

09:14.600 --> 09:15.560
Oh, wow!

09:16.960 --> 09:18.640
Thank you, everyone.

09:19.680 --> 09:22.200
All the best for the future.

09:24.160 --> 09:25.680
- Let's go.
- And, sir,

09:26.840 --> 09:28.680
your name is Mr...

09:28.800 --> 09:29.600
Gaurav.

09:29.920 --> 09:31.440
- "Gaurav."
- "Gaurav."

09:32.120 --> 09:33.160
Gaurav Dhar?

09:35.120 --> 09:36.560
So, Mr. Gaurav Dhar,

09:36.840 --> 09:38.960
had you been informed
about today's test?

09:39.160 --> 09:40.160
- No, sir.
- No?

09:40.400 --> 09:41.280
No, sir.

09:43.520 --> 09:46.440
Sir, I love machines,
not my position.

09:47.120 --> 09:49.840
Be it a printing press, fans,

09:50.560 --> 09:51.840
or complex machines like watches.

09:53.680 --> 09:55.160
- Good job.
- Well done.

09:55.480 --> 09:56.480
- Thank you.
- Look at this.

09:57.080 --> 09:58.320
Sir, am I...

10:03.640 --> 10:04.480
Sir?

10:06.080 --> 10:07.080
10 a.m. tomorrow.

10:10.000 --> 10:11.720
- Thank you. Sir, my hands...
- Uh-uh!

10:12.080 --> 10:13.240
- Okay.
- That's okay.

10:13.480 --> 10:15.560
- Welcome to the Watch Project.
- Thank you, sir.

10:15.840 --> 10:16.760
Whoa!

10:22.280 --> 10:24.280
We'll have to call a mechanic
along with an electrician.

10:24.320 --> 10:25.360
I'm used to it.

10:25.800 --> 10:27.240
Anyway, congratulations.

10:27.320 --> 10:28.320
See you tomorrow.

10:42.160 --> 10:43.520
[in Marathi] Hello, Megha.

10:43.880 --> 10:46.560
[in Marathi] Your mother
is truly proud of you.

10:46.560 --> 10:47.360
[in Marathi] But why?

10:47.400 --> 10:49.880
[in Marathi] This is the first time
someone has reached

10:49.880 --> 10:51.240
such great heights
in our neighbourhood.

10:51.320 --> 10:52.640
And Tata, no less!

10:58.800 --> 11:00.720
[in Marathi] Mom, is it true?

11:02.040 --> 11:02.840
Yes!

11:06.120 --> 11:08.680
Aunt Sheela got a call.

11:09.000 --> 11:10.480
You have to join
at 10 a.m. tomorrow.

11:16.400 --> 11:19.360
You won't have to run the packed
lunch service from tomorrow.

11:19.960 --> 11:21.080
You must rest now.

11:21.160 --> 11:23.200
- It doesn't work that way.
- Why not?

11:26.920 --> 11:28.800
- What should I do?
- No, leave it.

11:29.000 --> 11:30.160
I can do this.

11:30.320 --> 11:31.960
Malti's Subbu is waiting outside.

11:32.160 --> 11:33.080
Please go and meet him.

11:33.440 --> 11:36.320
You might even get
a marriage proposal.

11:36.520 --> 11:38.240
I don't want to marry, Mom.

11:38.320 --> 11:39.840
How many times should I tell you?

11:41.280 --> 11:42.520
At least meet him once.

11:43.440 --> 11:45.000
Please go. Please do as I say.

11:45.320 --> 11:46.320
Go and see him.

11:50.080 --> 11:51.000
Ms. Megha.

11:52.400 --> 11:53.720
Shall we go out for an ice cream?

11:57.840 --> 11:58.680
Yes?

11:59.200 --> 12:02.200
My name is Ravindra Naik,
and I suffer from flatulence.

12:03.880 --> 12:06.800
I mean, I'm a professor
at the J.J. School of Arts.

12:06.960 --> 12:08.560
Could you please call ma'am?

12:08.640 --> 12:10.520
Sorry, Mom can't make
any more packed lunches.

12:10.760 --> 12:12.600
But she agreed this morning.

12:16.040 --> 12:18.440
Mom, if you keep serving others,
when will you eat?

12:19.720 --> 12:21.120
I'm helpless.

12:21.400 --> 12:22.640
Otherwise, I would have eaten out.

12:22.840 --> 12:23.680
Okay.

12:23.960 --> 12:25.280
She'll cook for you every day,

12:25.320 --> 12:27.000
but she'll charge
four rupees per lunchbox.

12:27.560 --> 12:28.800
Are you doubling the rates?

12:28.960 --> 12:31.200
Since we're stretching our limits,
you should stretch yours too.

12:32.040 --> 12:35.000
Megha, he has a problem.

12:35.120 --> 12:37.120
So? What about your problems?

12:37.400 --> 12:39.600
We run a packed lunch service,
not a hospital, Mom.

12:40.520 --> 12:43.600
Tell me, sir.
Four rupees per lunchbox. Okay?

12:45.840 --> 12:47.160
Health is more important.

12:48.640 --> 12:51.160
Okay, I'll pay four rupees.

12:52.040 --> 12:53.760
Welcome to Sudha's Lunchbox Service.

12:54.600 --> 12:56.360
- Thank you.
- Welcome.

13:02.040 --> 13:04.120
Tell me, where do you want
to go for an ice cream?

13:05.000 --> 13:05.960
No! No!

13:07.480 --> 13:09.120
We can go later.

13:10.120 --> 13:11.600
The ice cream vendor
would still be there.

13:13.040 --> 13:13.840
Bye!

13:28.480 --> 13:29.520
Megha! Megha! Megha!

13:31.840 --> 13:33.400
Today is your first day at work,

13:33.800 --> 13:34.760
so this is for you.

13:35.640 --> 13:36.520
I'm running late.

13:38.760 --> 13:39.560
'Akash.'

13:39.640 --> 13:40.680
Kumud, I'm running late.

13:41.160 --> 13:42.160
'Akash.'

13:42.680 --> 13:43.680
- 'Akash!'
- Yes?

13:44.040 --> 13:45.640
At least have some
sweetened curd before you go.

13:45.960 --> 13:46.800
Oh!

13:47.680 --> 13:48.560
- All the best.
- Thank you!

13:48.640 --> 13:49.440
Bye!

13:51.960 --> 13:53.720
Hello, I'm Megha Mhatre.

13:54.440 --> 13:56.520
Hi! I'm Gaurav.

13:57.120 --> 14:00.320
Um... I was talking to him.

14:02.320 --> 14:03.880
Oh! Sorry!

14:04.120 --> 14:05.200
Mr. Gaurav Dhar?

14:06.120 --> 14:07.240
This is your ID card.

14:07.320 --> 14:08.240
Yes, thank you.

14:11.960 --> 14:13.240
You are...

14:13.680 --> 14:15.080
- Marketing.
- Okay.

14:17.120 --> 14:19.720
- And you?
- I'm the head engineer.

14:20.320 --> 14:21.240
Which college?

14:21.440 --> 14:22.480
IIT.

14:25.800 --> 14:27.960
Megha Mhatre, please take your card.

14:29.080 --> 14:30.440
Are you from IIM?

14:30.960 --> 14:32.360
No, I'm from Lady Shri Ram College.

14:35.840 --> 14:38.200
- Shall we?
- Yes, let's go. Please.

14:39.040 --> 14:40.560
- Excuse me, sir.
- Yes?

14:40.720 --> 14:41.760
- Your bag.
- Oh!

14:58.280 --> 14:59.160
He's joking.

14:59.360 --> 15:00.160
Oh.

15:00.400 --> 15:03.080
Megha, please help Akash
make the proposal.

15:03.200 --> 15:04.720
- Gaurav, please come here.
- Yes, sir.

15:05.000 --> 15:06.360
Sir, this was prepared by my mother.

15:06.560 --> 15:08.720
We cannot pitch today,
come what may.

15:08.800 --> 15:10.960
I can't say no
to the Tata Board, Akash.

15:12.280 --> 15:14.160
Hmm! This is amazing.

15:15.240 --> 15:16.520
- Zee.
- Yes?

15:16.600 --> 15:17.880
Our meeting
was scheduled for next month.

15:18.080 --> 15:18.920
We are not prepared yet.

15:18.960 --> 15:21.040
Yes, but it was brought forward,
so we have to prepare.

15:21.160 --> 15:22.560
That's that.

15:23.280 --> 15:24.080
Megha, come here.

15:24.120 --> 15:27.920
- Watch... A mechanical watch
has six main components. - Okay.

15:28.080 --> 15:29.560
- There's a barrel spring.
- Correct.

15:29.680 --> 15:31.160
It has a hand-setting mechanism.

15:31.240 --> 15:32.800
- And...
- Train wheels and cases.

15:33.280 --> 15:35.080
Oh! Very good!
You're one step ahead.

15:35.160 --> 15:36.960
Memorise all the other components.

15:37.040 --> 15:38.440
You'll need it for the pitch.

15:38.440 --> 15:39.400
What pitch, sir?

15:40.560 --> 15:41.640
The Watch Project pitch.

15:44.000 --> 15:47.240
Sir, is the Watch Project
not confirmed yet?

15:47.440 --> 15:49.640
Welcome
to the world of Xerxes Desai.

15:50.120 --> 15:52.480
We’re caught between a rock
and a hard place.

15:52.640 --> 15:53.760
Oi, you!

15:54.240 --> 15:55.240
Don't stress them out.

15:55.760 --> 15:58.200
- Okay.
- This is a manual on quartz.

15:58.600 --> 15:59.520
- "Quartz?"
- This... Yes.

15:59.600 --> 16:01.000
Go through it thoroughly.

16:01.080 --> 16:02.760
Be prepared
for any kind of question.

16:02.840 --> 16:04.440
These are the bullet points
for the feasibility report.

16:04.760 --> 16:05.920
You have two hours.

16:06.200 --> 16:07.920
Just fine-tune the entire proposal.

16:08.040 --> 16:10.960
Also, remember everything. Okay?
Take this.

16:12.080 --> 16:13.120
Only two hours, sir?

16:13.320 --> 16:14.680
Yes, is it a lot?

16:14.880 --> 16:18.080
It took us a year and a half
to collect this data.

16:18.200 --> 16:20.360
You just have to
write it beautifully.

16:20.440 --> 16:21.480
- You can do it.
- Okay?

16:23.880 --> 16:25.240
- Zee.
- Hmm?

16:25.360 --> 16:28.240
Please do as I say.
We don't even have any experts.

16:28.360 --> 16:29.360
We'll get them.

16:29.680 --> 16:31.760
- Loan?
- We'll get it.

16:34.640 --> 16:36.760
If we pitch unprepared,

16:36.840 --> 16:39.320
the entire Watch Project
might be cancelled.

16:40.640 --> 16:43.320
Can we request them
to delay this meeting?

16:44.200 --> 16:45.120
Please.

16:47.520 --> 16:48.360
Thanks.

16:49.160 --> 16:50.320
Hello, Operator.

16:51.000 --> 16:52.600
Please connect me to Bombay House,
Bombay.

16:53.000 --> 16:55.640
Yes, I'd like to speak to Mr. Tata.
Yes, J.R.D.

16:55.760 --> 16:56.560
J.R.D.

16:57.000 --> 16:57.920
Tell him.

16:59.080 --> 17:00.320
Tell him that we can't make it.

17:24.400 --> 17:25.320
- See you in five minutes.
- Yes.

17:35.640 --> 17:37.280
Don't be nervous.

17:38.200 --> 17:39.400
Go inside

17:40.120 --> 17:41.360
and convince them.

17:42.000 --> 17:43.080
Why don't you come with us?

17:43.160 --> 17:44.520
- No, I can't.
- Why not?

17:44.920 --> 17:47.480
The Board will accept
the Watch Project immediately.

17:47.600 --> 17:49.040
Everyone will listen to you.

17:49.120 --> 17:52.160
Zee, you have to convince them
through your potential,

17:52.240 --> 17:54.360
not through my status.

17:54.640 --> 17:58.440
Jeh, who took on the challenge
of making watches?

17:59.280 --> 18:00.760
"Symbol of excellence."

18:00.920 --> 18:04.480
Don't try
any of your 'Desaisms' on me.

18:05.360 --> 18:07.160
You must fight your own battle.

18:08.920 --> 18:09.760
Okay, tell me.

18:10.480 --> 18:12.400
What's the probability
of a yes or a no?

18:13.200 --> 18:15.840
- Fifty-fifty.
- Fifty-fifty means yes.

18:17.360 --> 18:18.400
You passed.

18:19.040 --> 18:20.200
What's the logic?

18:20.360 --> 18:24.360
The logic is that producing watches
is our dream.

18:27.040 --> 18:30.840
A dream without passion
and conviction is doomed to fail.

18:31.680 --> 18:33.400
If you can't convince them,

18:33.480 --> 18:36.080
how do you expect me
to entrust you with this company?

18:38.960 --> 18:39.800
Hmm?

18:41.240 --> 18:42.120
Come on.

18:54.560 --> 18:57.520
Collect all the watches
in the office

18:58.480 --> 18:59.480
and bring them to me.

18:59.720 --> 19:00.520
Why?

19:01.640 --> 19:02.680
No discussion,

19:04.280 --> 19:05.200
only demonstration.

19:06.040 --> 19:07.280
"All the watches."

19:07.720 --> 19:08.520
Zee.

19:12.920 --> 19:14.520
Hello! Good afternoon.

19:14.600 --> 19:15.760
Good afternoon, everyone.

19:16.600 --> 19:18.400
May I? Very nice!

19:19.880 --> 19:21.120
May I borrow your watch?

19:21.920 --> 19:23.080
Everyone's watch, please.

19:23.680 --> 19:26.560
Just give it to Gaurav
and Megha, please.

19:27.440 --> 19:28.840
Please humour me. Don't worry.

19:29.080 --> 19:30.160
I'll give them back.

19:37.720 --> 19:41.000
This box contains all the watches
from the entire building.

19:41.360 --> 19:45.040
My colleague
has also collected the clocks,

19:45.080 --> 19:46.360
which I didn't ask for.

19:46.840 --> 19:47.840
But...

19:49.240 --> 19:50.040
It's fine.

19:53.240 --> 19:54.200
Pulsar.

19:55.400 --> 19:56.280
Seiko.

19:56.560 --> 19:57.400
Citizen.

19:57.520 --> 19:58.480
Pulsar...

19:58.960 --> 20:00.680
What's the catch, Mr. Desai?

20:01.560 --> 20:03.040
The catch is that

20:03.680 --> 20:06.000
none of the watches
are made in India.

20:06.240 --> 20:07.760
Pick up the one in the corner.

20:08.200 --> 20:09.560
I wear a GMT watch.

20:09.760 --> 20:10.880
It's made in India.

20:12.520 --> 20:13.440
Fine.

20:14.280 --> 20:17.080
One watch is made in India.

20:17.320 --> 20:18.520
One watch out of...

20:20.200 --> 20:22.960
You cannot judge
the requirement of the whole country

20:23.080 --> 20:25.080
based on the requirement
of this room.

20:25.440 --> 20:26.360
We aren't.

20:35.360 --> 20:38.600
Sir, GMT manufactures
one million watches a year in India.

20:38.960 --> 20:41.680
Allwyn and other small companies
manufacture around 800,000 watches.

20:42.400 --> 20:44.840
The total number of watches
manufactured in India

20:44.920 --> 20:46.760
every year is 1.8 million.

20:47.640 --> 20:48.480
We know that.

20:48.840 --> 20:49.800
Yes, sir.

20:49.960 --> 20:52.320
But, sir, do you know
how many watches

20:52.400 --> 20:54.360
are sold in India every year?

20:55.600 --> 20:57.120
More than five million.

20:57.680 --> 21:00.800
The difference between
these two figures is 3.2 million.

21:01.240 --> 21:03.560
And the smugglers
are taking advantage of this gap.

21:03.640 --> 21:04.440
Yes.

21:04.520 --> 21:08.080
Yes, and these smuggled watches
are in demand

21:08.640 --> 21:11.200
because they upgrade with time.

21:11.680 --> 21:14.680
Which is exactly what we want to do.

21:15.160 --> 21:17.400
We want to dominate this market.

21:17.920 --> 21:20.800
Suppose watches are in demand,

21:21.240 --> 21:24.240
but you are looking at it
only in terms of sales.

21:24.400 --> 21:25.680
What about the first step,

21:26.160 --> 21:27.280
manufacturing?

21:28.000 --> 21:30.480
Sir, if GMT can, so can we.

21:30.560 --> 21:33.080
GMT has the best collaborators
in the world.

21:33.720 --> 21:34.680
It has Citizen.

21:34.880 --> 21:36.120
Allwyn has Seiko.

21:36.240 --> 21:37.800
Who do you have, Desai?

21:38.440 --> 21:39.920
We can find

21:41.480 --> 21:43.000
collaborators and experts, sir.

21:43.800 --> 21:46.280
It's a serious investment, Desai.

21:46.600 --> 21:47.520
I know.

21:48.080 --> 21:50.480
Which one do you have at the moment?

21:52.760 --> 21:54.120
At the moment, we...

21:58.520 --> 21:59.400
Sir!

22:00.600 --> 22:01.640
We trust Xerxes.

22:04.400 --> 22:06.560
The world doesn't run
on trust, Mr...

22:06.640 --> 22:07.480
Akash.

22:07.520 --> 22:08.840
Yes, Akash.

22:09.400 --> 22:11.800
The world runs on practicality.

22:14.560 --> 22:15.840
Sir, if we don't...

22:17.080 --> 22:17.920
Yes, sir.

22:24.280 --> 22:25.840
Let's take a break. Hmm?

22:27.120 --> 22:28.120
Thank you, sir.

22:50.200 --> 22:51.480
Excuse me, sirs.

22:52.240 --> 22:53.800
Have you seen the inside of a watch?

22:56.120 --> 22:57.200
Gaurav...

23:00.560 --> 23:01.960
This is a mechanical watch.

23:07.160 --> 23:08.200
Beautiful, right?

23:10.480 --> 23:11.640
But we won't make this.

23:13.160 --> 23:14.480
We will manufacture this one.

23:15.320 --> 23:17.160
I love mechanical watches,

23:17.400 --> 23:19.880
but I'll 'marry' quartz.

23:20.240 --> 23:21.400
See. Here...

23:21.840 --> 23:23.680
That's the quartz crystal.

23:24.680 --> 23:25.840
You want to produce watches

23:25.920 --> 23:29.000
and even experiment
with new technology?

23:29.120 --> 23:29.960
Yes, sir.

23:30.600 --> 23:32.280
- Because quartz is the future.
- Yes!

23:32.520 --> 23:33.640
It really is.

23:35.200 --> 23:37.760
GMT primarily manufactures
mechanical watches.

23:38.360 --> 23:39.880
They hardly produce quartz watches.

23:40.480 --> 23:42.120
I'm sure they have a good reason.

23:42.480 --> 23:43.440
Maybe.

23:44.560 --> 23:46.640
Or maybe they aren't even thinking.

23:48.280 --> 23:50.880
That's because
they don't have any competition.

23:51.920 --> 23:54.720
But our designs and technology

23:55.720 --> 23:58.640
will revolutionise the way
Indians think about luxury.

24:00.640 --> 24:02.040
They sell watches,

24:02.640 --> 24:05.680
but we'll sell dreams
to every Indian.

24:12.320 --> 24:14.480
Sir, your watch is dead.

24:25.720 --> 24:28.720
Sir, mechanical watches
are beautiful,

24:28.960 --> 24:31.040
but they need to be
wound repeatedly.

24:31.760 --> 24:34.120
Your time is precious, Mr. Singh.

24:34.200 --> 24:36.280
You can't afford to lose
track of time like this.

24:37.560 --> 24:39.280
That's why we have to move on.

24:40.000 --> 24:42.960
We have to move on
to this self-sustaining technology.

24:45.680 --> 24:46.600
Gaurav...

24:50.400 --> 24:53.480
Sir, we need 120 to 180 components

24:53.760 --> 24:56.640
to produce a mechanical watch.

24:57.080 --> 25:00.800
On the other hand, a quartz watch
requires only 60 to 70 components.

25:01.400 --> 25:02.920
It's a simple technology.

25:03.000 --> 25:06.880
This is why its manufacturing cost
and time will be much lower, sir.

25:07.520 --> 25:08.760
We don't have to do much.

25:08.960 --> 25:11.680
Look at the battery.
Quartz watches run on batteries.

25:12.160 --> 25:13.280
Just take the battery

25:15.800 --> 25:16.640
and...

25:17.720 --> 25:18.720
That's it, sir.

25:19.600 --> 25:20.960
It will function smoothly
for two to three years.

25:21.320 --> 25:22.360
Well done.

25:25.480 --> 25:30.280
Desai, if you truly want to start
a new venture, choose a safe one.

25:30.720 --> 25:32.400
Go for large-scale manufacturing,

25:32.640 --> 25:35.360
like Tata Steel and Tata Motors.

25:35.600 --> 25:36.520
Go big!

25:36.560 --> 25:37.400
We are Tatas.

25:37.480 --> 25:39.440
Exactly, sir. Exactly!

25:39.920 --> 25:41.440
We are Tatas.

25:41.840 --> 25:45.520
If we don't create history,
who will?

25:45.800 --> 25:49.720
Creating history is one thing,
and becoming history is another.

25:50.000 --> 25:53.320
I hope you understand
what we are afraid of, Mr. Desai.

25:54.000 --> 25:55.760
Since when did we
start being afraid?

25:56.840 --> 26:00.400
Mr. Jamsetji Tata was the founder
of India's first steel plant,

26:01.440 --> 26:03.320
which was subsequently started
by Mr. Dorabji Tata.

26:03.960 --> 26:06.680
The British made fun of him
and ridiculed his abilities.

26:07.680 --> 26:10.520
Yet he sold them steel during the
First World War, making a profit.

26:12.320 --> 26:14.360
When Jamsetji was denied
entry to the Watson Hotel,

26:14.400 --> 26:17.240
where the noticeboard read,
"Dogs and Indians are not allowed",

26:18.320 --> 26:22.400
he went on to create Asia's biggest
luxury five-star hotel chain.

26:24.080 --> 26:25.320
The Taj Mahal Palace,

26:25.880 --> 26:27.480
equipped
with the first electric lift.

26:28.720 --> 26:30.760
Sir, we knew nothing
about consumerism,

26:30.840 --> 26:32.920
yet we launched
Tata Tea and Tata Salt.

26:33.000 --> 26:36.920
Today, the whole nation
wakes up with our tea.

26:41.720 --> 26:43.720
What about the IT industry, Akash?

26:44.200 --> 26:45.000
Yes, sir.

26:45.080 --> 26:48.080
We had no knowledge
of information technology.

26:48.760 --> 26:51.200
Yet TCS has been making
a profit for the past 12 years.

26:52.960 --> 26:54.960
Sir, we've travelled
through the sky.

26:55.920 --> 26:57.640
Can't we manufacture a watch?

27:01.560 --> 27:02.800
Thank you, Akash.

27:05.280 --> 27:08.400
Sometimes, it takes a new face
to remind us of our history.

27:10.960 --> 27:14.440
Besides, Mr. Singh,
we are sticking with the engine.

27:16.000 --> 27:20.080
This watch is the smallest engine
in the world.

27:22.200 --> 27:23.920
It is a marvel.

27:30.320 --> 27:31.880
No offence, gentlemen,

27:32.520 --> 27:34.200
but if I were in your place,

27:35.760 --> 27:37.520
I would put my career,

27:37.840 --> 27:42.320
my life, my everything
at stake for this project.

27:47.120 --> 27:48.400
We should have a quick vote.

27:48.680 --> 27:50.560
Those in favour
of the Watch Project,

27:51.040 --> 27:52.040
raise your hands.

28:19.480 --> 28:21.440
Those who are not in favour,
please raise your hands.

28:39.200 --> 28:40.520
You've got a tie.

28:50.320 --> 28:51.280
But

28:52.760 --> 28:55.240
looking at your passion for quartz,

28:56.480 --> 28:58.560
I cast you my vote, Desai.

29:06.920 --> 29:08.120
I've seen your report,

29:09.040 --> 29:12.280
and it's clear that you need
substantial funding.

29:12.920 --> 29:15.000
KBI will definitely give you a loan.

29:15.680 --> 29:19.560
Please send your licence proposal
to the government for approval.

29:20.480 --> 29:21.720
All the best.

29:22.840 --> 29:23.880
Thank you, sir.

29:25.160 --> 29:26.040
Thank you.

29:27.920 --> 29:28.920
So?

29:30.360 --> 29:31.480
What's the decision?

29:32.480 --> 29:33.720
51%.

29:36.200 --> 29:38.320
Sir, the Watch Project
is good to go.

29:39.400 --> 29:40.520
Congratulations!

29:42.160 --> 29:43.800
Sorry, I was a little late.

29:46.080 --> 29:47.200
But you can't be late.

30:11.760 --> 30:12.920
- Zee.
- Hmm?

30:13.040 --> 30:16.120
I drafted the licence application.
Please review before applying.

30:19.120 --> 30:21.440
Please do come and feel at home.

30:21.640 --> 30:23.000
Do you eat here nowadays?

30:23.920 --> 30:26.600
The food goes cold
by the time it reaches home.

30:26.960 --> 30:29.520
Your mom suggested I eat here.

30:30.400 --> 30:32.480
Why did you make 'laddus'?

30:32.720 --> 30:34.920
You've received a marriage proposal
from an IPS officer.

30:37.240 --> 30:38.680
Whether or not our watches
get manufactured,

30:38.760 --> 30:40.600
you want me to marry. Am I right?

30:41.760 --> 30:44.520
'How will you live alone
after I'm gone, Megha?'

30:44.640 --> 30:47.560
Many people live alone in Bombay.
I can too.

30:47.880 --> 30:50.240
I won't marry
just for the sake of company.

30:50.320 --> 30:52.480
What if I lose my job
because of my marriage?

30:52.520 --> 30:54.600
You'd be burdened once again.

30:54.920 --> 30:55.920
"Burden?"

30:56.400 --> 30:57.560
Don't say that, my dear.

30:57.920 --> 30:59.640
Why don't you understand, Mom?

30:59.920 --> 31:02.520
A woman has no identity
without marriage, my child.

31:06.480 --> 31:07.920
How could you say that, Mom?

32:10.560 --> 32:12.000
Has our proposal been rejected?

32:14.520 --> 32:15.600
We'll find a way.

32:16.320 --> 32:18.040
Zee, I don't want to lose this job.

32:18.880 --> 32:20.960
- Ever since I left NBIDC...
- Yes! Yes.

32:21.360 --> 32:22.480
You've mentioned it.

32:23.280 --> 32:25.040
I was talking to Kumud
and Dad last night,

32:25.040 --> 32:27.080
- and I was...
- I have a family too, Akash.

32:27.760 --> 32:30.920
But Tata will assign you
to another project.

32:30.960 --> 32:32.720
- What about me?
- Let me think.

32:35.440 --> 32:36.840
Why are you avoiding me?

32:37.640 --> 32:39.160
Your friend
is asking you a question.

32:39.200 --> 32:40.080
"Friend?"

32:40.920 --> 32:43.480
What responsibility
did you fulfil as a friend?

32:44.800 --> 32:47.680
It was your job to read the
government regulations, wasn't it?

32:48.000 --> 32:49.800
How could you miss the MRTP Act?

32:52.840 --> 32:54.200
Didn't I fulfil my responsibility?

32:54.240 --> 32:55.040
Yes.

32:55.840 --> 32:57.560
What about your responsibilities?

32:57.880 --> 33:00.040
Loans and experts were supposed
to be brought by you.

33:00.080 --> 33:00.880
Where are they?

33:00.960 --> 33:03.120
We were not rejected
for either loans or experts.

33:03.720 --> 33:06.040
We were rejected
because of the MRTP Act.

33:06.120 --> 33:08.840
Come on!
Don't pretend it was all my fault.

33:08.840 --> 33:09.640
It is!

33:09.720 --> 33:11.160
The Watch Project was your idea,

33:11.640 --> 33:12.960
and there has been a mistake in it.

33:13.400 --> 33:16.440
If the core is wrong,
there's no point in covering it up.

33:17.040 --> 33:20.000
I stood by you,
believing in your idea.

33:20.120 --> 33:21.280
But what did you do?

33:21.600 --> 33:23.440
You keep talking
about family and job,

33:23.600 --> 33:25.000
yet you couldn't even do
your one job!

33:25.480 --> 33:26.320
I don't even know

33:26.400 --> 33:28.440
what your contribution
to the Watch Project is!

33:41.600 --> 33:42.560
I'm sorry, I...

33:43.960 --> 33:45.040
I didn't mean that...

33:47.760 --> 33:49.240
This sorry...

33:51.480 --> 33:52.760
Is it from a friend or a boss?

33:52.960 --> 33:54.960
What boss? I'm your friend.

33:57.640 --> 33:59.040
I forgive my friend.

34:00.280 --> 34:01.320
But, Zee,

34:03.760 --> 34:04.760
I quit.

34:10.120 --> 34:13.680
I can't work under such uncertainty

34:15.280 --> 34:16.440
with a boss like that.

34:20.200 --> 34:21.640
I'm sorry, Zee.

34:22.520 --> 34:23.560
I quit.

34:43.120 --> 34:44.400
It's just a single rejection.

34:44.720 --> 34:46.000
"A single rejection?"

34:47.640 --> 34:49.840
The project is dead
before it even started.

35:02.720 --> 35:04.920
they needed lifts.

35:05.600 --> 35:08.040
But the lifts were too slow.

35:08.680 --> 35:11.280
The person waiting
for the lift would get bored,

35:11.360 --> 35:15.800
and the one inside
would feel claustrophobic.

35:16.000 --> 35:19.880
- Hmm. - The plan to build
skyscrapers was in jeopardy.

35:21.160 --> 35:23.560
Who would buy a flat
on the 50th or 60th floor

35:23.640 --> 35:26.520
of a building without a lift?

35:27.440 --> 35:28.600
- Right?
- Right.

35:29.200 --> 35:30.240
So,

35:31.120 --> 35:32.240
do you know what they did?

35:32.800 --> 35:35.000
Did they build high-speed lifts?

35:36.160 --> 35:38.360
That technology
was still years away.

35:39.440 --> 35:44.240
They installed mirrors in the lifts.

35:44.360 --> 35:46.000
- Mirrors.
- All right.

35:46.400 --> 35:48.320
So that one could see one's face,

35:48.400 --> 35:52.080
adjust one's clothes,
set one's hair,

35:52.120 --> 35:53.920
and reach one's floor
before even realising it.

35:54.480 --> 35:55.280
Right.

35:55.560 --> 35:57.080
Such a simple solution

35:57.280 --> 35:58.760
to a serious problem.

36:00.320 --> 36:01.240
Right?

36:01.760 --> 36:05.600
I'm sure you'll find
your own 'mirror' too.

36:06.200 --> 36:07.480
But today,

36:09.080 --> 36:10.760
your only challenge

36:11.080 --> 36:12.800
is to beat me.

36:15.000 --> 36:16.040
Come on!

36:25.760 --> 36:26.760
Dad.

36:28.080 --> 36:29.400
- Dad!
- Hmm?

36:30.240 --> 36:31.520
The tea has turned cold.

36:31.840 --> 36:33.080
And please eat something.

36:33.480 --> 36:34.360
Okay?

36:40.520 --> 36:43.600
Are you happy working at NBIDC?

36:43.680 --> 36:45.320
I work for Tata, Dad.

36:46.920 --> 36:47.960
I mean, I used to.

36:48.800 --> 36:51.440
Please eat something.

36:52.200 --> 36:55.040
Are you happy where you are?

36:58.040 --> 36:59.800
- No.
- Why?

37:00.720 --> 37:01.960
Because of Xerxes.

37:02.800 --> 37:04.840
The man who came
for lunch the other day.

37:05.600 --> 37:07.600
Do you remember my senior at NBIDC?

37:08.360 --> 37:10.760
I used to say he had
a solution to every problem.

37:12.600 --> 37:15.240
I thought he could cure
even my boredom.

37:15.840 --> 37:17.520
That's why I followed him
and joined Tata.

37:18.560 --> 37:21.080
But after coming here,
I realised he was crazy.

37:22.040 --> 37:23.560
Although he had left NBIDC,

37:23.680 --> 37:24.800
he didn't sit still.

37:24.960 --> 37:26.680
He had a simple desk job,

37:26.760 --> 37:28.240
but he wanted a challenge.

37:29.000 --> 37:31.000
If he really wanted
to start a new venture,

37:31.160 --> 37:32.640
he could have chosen a safe one.

37:32.760 --> 37:34.000
But no.

37:34.600 --> 37:35.840
What did he choose?

37:36.320 --> 37:37.920
Watch manufacturing.

37:40.880 --> 37:42.320
There was so much pressure

37:42.560 --> 37:44.120
that I couldn't handle it.

37:48.600 --> 37:51.920
Strangely, despite the chaos
of working with him,

37:57.640 --> 37:59.400
I enjoyed it a lot.

38:06.920 --> 38:08.920
They suddenly gave me
a kind of relief,

38:09.840 --> 38:12.600
after a life
that had been so boring.

38:14.680 --> 38:18.280
Have you gone mad like him?

38:23.000 --> 38:24.000
Yes, Dad.

38:25.760 --> 38:27.840
That company
is full of insane people.

38:28.960 --> 38:30.720
Perhaps I've become one of them.

38:31.600 --> 38:34.320
I work for the passion,
not the money.

38:35.560 --> 38:37.080
I guess, yes. I...

38:38.920 --> 38:40.080
I've gone crazy.

38:42.920 --> 38:44.920
And maybe I can't live

38:47.480 --> 38:48.920
without the craziness.

38:58.520 --> 38:59.960
Thanks, Dad.

39:10.800 --> 39:11.720
Water!

39:17.320 --> 39:18.600
Do you need more?

39:21.200 --> 39:22.200
I've found the solution.

39:23.000 --> 39:23.800
What is it?

39:24.560 --> 39:25.640
The MRTP Act.

39:25.840 --> 39:27.440
That's the problem, Akash.

39:27.520 --> 39:29.520
It's the solution too. Listen.

39:30.080 --> 39:31.400
According to the MRTP Act,

39:31.480 --> 39:34.360
large-scale companies aren't allowed
to manufacture watches, right?

39:34.520 --> 39:37.880
- Right. - But there's no mention
of whether a sister company

39:37.960 --> 39:41.720
or a company funded by a large
corporation can enter the market.

39:43.680 --> 39:46.680
What if we don't enter
the market as the Tatas,

39:46.840 --> 39:50.360
but as an investment company
under Tata?

39:57.960 --> 39:59.160
Hello, Operator?

39:59.840 --> 40:01.080
Please connect me to Madras.

40:02.560 --> 40:05.120
The number is 6246004.

40:05.240 --> 40:07.720
- Do you need more?
- One more glass, please.

40:07.840 --> 40:08.880
Shankar?

40:20.520 --> 40:22.960
Come on, it's really good.

40:30.240 --> 40:32.040
You want to convince
TIDCO's chairman

40:33.800 --> 40:34.720
with a 'laddu'?

40:34.800 --> 40:36.200
No, it's not like that.

40:38.320 --> 40:39.480
Is it working, though?

40:41.000 --> 40:42.680
- It's good.
- Hmm.

40:43.680 --> 40:46.440
Why not Maharashtra
or any other state?

40:46.800 --> 40:48.160
Any state can give you land.

40:48.440 --> 40:50.000
You gave me the idea of watches,

40:50.040 --> 40:52.360
so why should we give the profit
from a land deal to someone else?

40:56.760 --> 40:59.840
I would've signed the deal
immediately if it were in my hands,

41:01.160 --> 41:02.760
but the minister won't agree.

41:03.560 --> 41:04.480
Why, sir?

41:05.360 --> 41:07.440
He doesn't trust capitalists.

41:13.240 --> 41:15.000
I can arrange a meeting with him.

41:19.880 --> 41:20.680
But he won't agree.

41:23.960 --> 41:24.800
"TIDCO!"

41:26.200 --> 41:27.000
It's good.

41:27.240 --> 41:28.720
I could really use
your help here, Jeh.

41:29.320 --> 41:30.520
The minister

41:31.280 --> 41:32.720
apparently hates capitalists.

41:32.880 --> 41:35.680
- Whoa! Really?
- Yes.

41:36.440 --> 41:38.200
We have a meeting with him
the day after tomorrow at 2 p.m.

41:39.280 --> 41:41.520
Well, book us on the 9 a.m. flight.

41:43.560 --> 41:44.400
Great!

41:51.760 --> 41:52.600
Hello!

41:53.240 --> 41:54.680
Rishabh, you need
to understand one thing.

41:54.760 --> 41:57.000
When you're dealing with me,
please be clear

41:57.000 --> 41:58.720
with the numbers,
because I am. Locked.

41:58.960 --> 41:59.840
Thank you, Rishabh.

42:00.240 --> 42:02.480
- Sir, you called us urgently.
- Hmm.

42:03.800 --> 42:05.520
All okay, sir?

42:07.080 --> 42:08.560
No, you're fired.

42:12.960 --> 42:14.680
Sir, you are just...

42:15.720 --> 42:16.680
Yes.

42:16.880 --> 42:18.160
Your termination letters.

42:21.200 --> 42:22.040
Sorry, guys.

42:22.400 --> 42:23.560
- Sir, but what happened?
- Sir...

42:23.880 --> 42:25.000
Stop it!

42:26.760 --> 42:27.720
Sir, sorry?

42:28.080 --> 42:29.280
You're fired,

42:30.280 --> 42:32.760
because you're hired
in our new company.

42:36.680 --> 42:38.640
- Okay.
- Sir...

42:42.480 --> 42:44.080
Who are Questar Investments?

42:44.480 --> 42:47.360
Well, we're now
a small independent investment firm.

42:48.760 --> 42:49.600
Yes!

42:49.640 --> 42:52.480
How is a small investment firm

42:53.040 --> 42:54.800
supposed to compete with GMT?

42:54.880 --> 42:57.080
We're a small independent
investment firm

42:57.680 --> 42:59.200
backed by the Tatas.

43:01.240 --> 43:04.440
Just because our firm is small,
that doesn't diminish

43:04.920 --> 43:07.120
our thinking or our dreams.

43:08.640 --> 43:09.480
Right?

43:09.960 --> 43:10.840
Right, sir.

43:11.400 --> 43:12.520
What's the time?

43:12.880 --> 43:14.480
- Sir, 8:30.
- It's 8:30, sir.

43:14.920 --> 43:16.360
- It's 8:30.
- Fine.

43:18.000 --> 43:19.880
You two don't wear watches?

43:20.000 --> 43:21.640
Because we haven't made one yet.

43:35.400 --> 43:36.960
Welcome to Questar Investments.

43:37.120 --> 43:38.000
Thank you, sir.

43:38.040 --> 43:39.520
- Thank you, sir.
- It's a pleasure.

43:55.680 --> 43:56.560
Nervous?

43:56.800 --> 43:58.680
I just really want this to go well.

43:59.320 --> 44:02.600
You know, Zee,
you have a basic problem.

44:03.440 --> 44:04.280
Which one?

44:04.360 --> 44:05.880
Whatever comes to your mind

44:07.000 --> 44:09.000
shows clearly on your face.

44:09.800 --> 44:10.800
Oh!

44:11.840 --> 44:16.440
You should keep this in mind.
When you meet a client,

44:17.040 --> 44:19.600
you should keep a straight face.

44:19.960 --> 44:21.720
- "A straight face?"
- Yes.

44:22.880 --> 44:27.040
I've started referring to
a Hindi dictionary, inspired by you.

44:28.440 --> 44:29.800
A straight face

44:30.120 --> 44:32.120
means an expressionless face.

44:32.320 --> 44:33.920
- Oh!
- No expression.

44:37.880 --> 44:38.880
- Hmm?
- Hmm.

44:39.440 --> 44:41.600
The client should know nothing

44:42.240 --> 44:44.760
about what's in your head.

44:46.320 --> 44:49.560
If you laugh first,
he'll take you for granted.

44:50.720 --> 44:54.320
If he sees that you're nervous,
he'll underestimate you.

44:57.760 --> 44:59.040
Always remember this.

45:01.360 --> 45:05.440
Your face shouldn't show
a single wrinkle.

45:08.680 --> 45:10.760
But your face has so many wrinkles.

45:16.520 --> 45:19.320
Ah! Touché.

45:21.320 --> 45:22.480
- Shankar.
- Sir?

45:22.520 --> 45:23.880
[in Tamil] Are you serious?

45:24.320 --> 45:25.680
[in Tamil]
I won't give away our lands

45:25.720 --> 45:27.720
for their profit.

45:27.880 --> 45:30.360
[in Tamil] Sir, please wait
at least until the meeting.

45:30.600 --> 45:32.960
They are the ones
making us wait right now.

45:33.040 --> 45:35.200
The appointment is at 2 p.m., sir.

45:35.440 --> 45:36.560
Good afternoon, gentlemen.

45:36.680 --> 45:38.000
I trust we're on time.

45:38.360 --> 45:39.360
Right, Xerxes?

45:41.960 --> 45:42.960
Yes, sir.

45:43.080 --> 45:44.960
Did you also stop wearing a watch?

45:45.080 --> 45:45.960
Yes, sir.

45:46.120 --> 45:47.040
Sir, please.

45:47.160 --> 45:48.120
Thank you!

45:52.040 --> 45:55.000
I apologise,
but we're a little short of time.

45:55.720 --> 45:57.840
So, if you don't mind, we should

45:58.120 --> 46:00.400
discuss the terms and conditions
of the agreement now.

46:00.480 --> 46:01.760
What terms and conditions?

46:02.440 --> 46:03.880
We didn't agree
to give away our land.

46:04.000 --> 46:06.960
Not your terms and conditions,
I'm talking about ours.

46:07.480 --> 46:09.440
In exchange for the land,

46:10.400 --> 46:12.680
I'm offering you a collaboration

46:13.520 --> 46:15.480
between TIDCO and the Tatas.

46:16.160 --> 46:17.440
"TIDCO and the Tatas?"

46:18.640 --> 46:20.160
"TIDCO and the Tatas?"

46:23.040 --> 46:25.480
And in that collaboration,

46:25.600 --> 46:28.680
27.88% of the stakes

46:28.920 --> 46:30.680
will belong to TIDCO.

46:31.760 --> 46:32.960
Stakes, Jeh?

46:35.600 --> 46:36.440
Sir.

46:37.520 --> 46:39.680
That's almost 28%.

46:43.680 --> 46:45.400
Are you serious or joking?

46:46.240 --> 46:48.520
I never joke when I
talk about business.

46:48.920 --> 46:51.880
We're not here
just for the land or the factories.

46:52.000 --> 46:54.560
I want to start an industry.

46:56.240 --> 46:59.960
It will benefit the people
of Tamil Nadu, not just us,

47:00.800 --> 47:04.840
because we will employ only locals.

47:05.480 --> 47:07.000
So, employment,

47:08.200 --> 47:11.760
stakes, collaboration,
and the Tatas.

47:12.440 --> 47:14.040
What more incentive do you need?

47:14.520 --> 47:15.360
[in Tamil] Sir,

47:16.280 --> 47:18.760
other state governments

47:19.080 --> 47:20.640
would jump at the chance.

47:34.240 --> 47:35.880
Akash, give him the MOU.

47:39.960 --> 47:41.560
What's wrong with your face?

47:43.600 --> 47:44.960
A straight face!

47:47.680 --> 47:49.440
[in Gujarati]
Do you need anything else?

47:49.560 --> 47:52.640
[in Gujarati] And where
did you learn Gujarati?

47:52.760 --> 47:55.440
[in Gujarati] Tell me quickly.
Do you need anything?

47:55.640 --> 47:59.120
A minimum of one year's training
with French collaborators.

47:59.840 --> 48:00.920
You took the words
right out of my mouth.

48:01.000 --> 48:02.400
And they must undertake

48:02.760 --> 48:06.160
one year of training
with French experts.

48:06.400 --> 48:07.680
- Fine.
- Sir.

48:15.920 --> 48:18.760
No, not me. Xerxes is the founder.

48:22.840 --> 48:23.720
Sign it.

48:54.640 --> 48:56.560
Who will be your GM?

48:57.200 --> 48:59.200
Shyama Krishna Gopalan.

48:59.760 --> 49:01.480
- When is he expected?
- Any minute now.

49:02.560 --> 49:04.560
He seems to be

49:05.280 --> 49:06.320
a serious person.

49:06.400 --> 49:07.840
Focus on his work,
not his appearance.

49:08.760 --> 49:09.840
His strategies

49:10.120 --> 49:12.200
worked wonders
at Belfast Electronics.

49:12.280 --> 49:13.360
- No, really.
- Look.

49:13.440 --> 49:14.640
Look at his face.

49:15.160 --> 49:19.160
It seems he'll come over and say,
"Hi, this is Shyama Krishna Gopalan.

49:19.520 --> 49:23.680
S.K. Gopalan. Are you Xerox Desai?"

49:25.080 --> 49:26.080
Hello!

49:26.520 --> 49:27.680
You are

49:27.880 --> 49:31.880
Mr. 'Xerzex' Desai?

49:32.720 --> 49:36.000
Actually, I'm Xerxes,
but you can call me Zee or Desai.

49:36.600 --> 49:37.720
I would prefer "Mr. Desai".

49:37.920 --> 49:38.760
Please!

49:40.160 --> 49:41.040
Thank you.

49:43.240 --> 49:45.920
I happen to be

49:46.760 --> 49:47.960
S.K. Gopalan.

49:48.200 --> 49:49.000
Yes.

49:49.760 --> 49:50.880
Welcome to the Watch Project.

49:50.960 --> 49:52.200
Oh, thank you. Thank you so much.

49:52.360 --> 49:53.640
Um...

49:53.880 --> 49:57.640
Is there no formal name
for the company yet?

50:16.920 --> 50:17.800
Gaurav.

50:18.880 --> 50:19.680
Idea?

50:23.400 --> 50:27.840
I think it should be
something mythological.

50:28.240 --> 50:30.600
- Megha? - Can we think
of something different, sir?

50:31.040 --> 50:33.720
- Like Nike, the Greek Goddess.
- No!

50:34.280 --> 50:36.720
There are thousands of brands
with mythological names.

50:37.560 --> 50:38.600
Think of something else.

50:45.040 --> 50:47.840
Volkswagen means
"people's car" in German.

50:47.920 --> 50:50.320
If we want to say, "people's watch",

50:51.280 --> 50:52.760
it could be 'Lokghadi'.

50:54.960 --> 50:56.360
It's an atrocious idea.

50:56.440 --> 50:57.400
- No! No!
- Sorry! Chuck it.

50:57.800 --> 50:59.360
Think of an easy name

51:00.000 --> 51:01.640
that reflects our brand value.

51:02.920 --> 51:04.120
Uh, Gopalan.

51:04.640 --> 51:06.520
- It's a government letter.
- Thank you.

51:19.320 --> 51:21.120
We finally got the licence.

51:21.440 --> 51:22.600
Is it done?

51:24.280 --> 51:25.160
Phew!

51:27.360 --> 51:29.360
- So taking it from there...
- Hmm.

51:29.520 --> 51:33.120
I was thinking, Nescafé got its name

51:33.240 --> 51:36.000
- from its parent company,
Nestlé, right? - Hmm.

51:36.760 --> 51:38.400
And what is our parent company?

51:46.680 --> 51:48.120
- Tata Industries?
- Hmm.

51:48.360 --> 51:50.000
And our partner is...

51:53.600 --> 51:54.840
TIDCO.

51:55.440 --> 51:58.240
So what if we derive
something from these two...

51:58.360 --> 52:00.800
- Don't you think
this name is too long? - Entities.

52:01.600 --> 52:03.440
Not ours.

52:12.960 --> 52:15.560
- Tata Industries Tamil Nadu.
- We can work on it.

52:15.840 --> 52:16.680
No.

52:20.760 --> 52:22.680
We need a name

52:22.960 --> 52:25.440
that represents
our strength, legacy,

52:25.800 --> 52:27.320
and ambition.

52:27.600 --> 52:28.400
- Right?
- Yes, sir.

52:28.440 --> 52:29.240
I agree.

52:56.680 --> 52:57.600
Titan.

52:59.960 --> 53:01.160
Mr. Desai...

53:01.600 --> 53:02.480
Hmm?

53:03.160 --> 53:05.200
That's so nice.

53:07.720 --> 53:09.600
- Man!
- Well done!

53:09.920 --> 53:12.080
- Congratulations!
- Sir, it's perfect.

53:12.200 --> 53:13.920
Oh, good! Nice?

53:14.360 --> 53:15.320
- It's nice.
- Is it?

53:15.400 --> 53:16.400
- Yes.
- Right?

53:17.680 --> 53:18.840
It's good.

53:20.720 --> 53:21.600
'Titan?'

53:21.960 --> 53:23.120
- Yes.
- Hmm.

53:24.280 --> 53:25.360
I've never heard it before.

53:25.880 --> 53:29.080
The company is registered,
but it hasn't been established yet.

53:29.560 --> 53:30.720
Then why do you need a loan?

53:31.400 --> 53:34.160
To establish the company.

53:34.960 --> 53:38.000
You see, we've had a long-standing
relationship with the Tatas.

53:38.080 --> 53:38.960
- Hmm.
- Yes.

53:39.280 --> 53:41.280
But producing watches
is a risky business.

53:41.640 --> 53:42.480
Well...

53:42.560 --> 53:45.200
On top of that, you want to
manufacture quartz watches, right?

53:45.320 --> 53:46.280
Yes.

53:46.480 --> 53:50.520
It contributes only 5%
to GMT's total sales.

53:50.600 --> 53:53.440
- Yes, because they focus on...
- Do you know something?

53:53.720 --> 53:56.120
Why is people's money
safe in our bank?

53:58.400 --> 54:00.440
Not because of tight security,

54:00.880 --> 54:04.200
but because we never
put their money at risk.

54:04.320 --> 54:05.360
Yes... No.

54:05.720 --> 54:08.880
- Sir, I know it's a bit...
- I'm sorry, Mr. Desai.

54:10.080 --> 54:12.440
If any other bank
is willing to take the risk,

54:12.800 --> 54:13.800
all the best,

54:14.360 --> 54:16.080
but we cannot grant you a loan.

54:18.560 --> 54:19.640
I'm sorry.

54:26.880 --> 54:29.840
'Sorry, Mr. Desai. We cannot
grant your company a loan.'

54:30.560 --> 54:32.400
'Your loan application
has been rejected.'

54:33.160 --> 54:35.000
'No one will understand
this technology.'

54:35.080 --> 54:36.960
'Quartz? What is that?'

54:39.000 --> 54:41.120
'We are not ready to invest in you.
Sorry!'

54:42.600 --> 54:44.280
'I'm sorry,
your loan has been rejected.'

54:45.040 --> 54:46.920
'This technology is rather new.'

54:47.120 --> 54:49.520
'Sorry, Mr. Desai.
We can't grant you a loan.'

54:49.600 --> 54:52.240
'- People won't understand it.
- Your loan has been rejected.'

54:52.640 --> 54:55.080
'- Sorry, Mr. Desai.
- Sorry!'

56:54.080 --> 56:54.920
---
